From 2becd4fa08012a044d73ad471914e0013753d84d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:42:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] device: drop damaged video up to the next key frame

A hardware decoder may hang or fail on an incomplete frame, e.g. the
Amlogic decoder after lost TS packets at the start of VDR. VDR passes a
PES with lost packets on.

Play the TS packets one by one to assign a lost or damaged video packet
to its PES. With a hardware decoder drop the damaged frame and the
following frames, which may refer to it, up to the next key frame and
restart the decoder there like at a new stream.

The new option DropDamagedVideo enables it, by default automatically
with the new hardware quirk of the Amlogic SoCs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
